{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/1627","id":5157229158,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQ8oa8s8AAAABM2USZg","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1627","diff_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1627.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1627.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/1627","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/1627/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/1627/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/1627/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/statuses/89efe190ba97d50de1fc8f73a523e992ed3e91b2","number":1627,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[I17:E03] Delivery Lanes: Each Task Row Carries Its Lane","user":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Overview\n\nTask rows carry a board-wide Lane index after Joins and before Done. A Lane artifact owns its rules and operations, with one module for assignment, validation, unit consistency and request admission. Planning, delivery, dependency checks, issue formatting and queue reporting consume that owner.\n\n## Changes\n\nLane has one subject contract and shared implementation; the full epic integrates these behaviors.\n\n### Lane Ownership\n\n- **Artifact operations.**\n  Lane owns reading, confirmed assignment, unit checks and admission; Epic Issue Body owns the table shape and delegates assignment.\n- **Shared implementation.**\n  Focused Lane functions serve all consumers, while board-derived state/grouping lives in Board below delivery and queue entry points.\n\n### Task Tables\n\n- **Raw row indices.**\n  Bare opaque decimal strings preserve spelling; empty cells are unlaned, and work items describe Component.\n- **Preserved row data.**\n  Formatting, reservation/release, delivery linking and completion preserve Lane values by task.\n- **Bounded validation.**\n  Markup/prose, missing joined assignments and split units produce diagnostics; unsupported cross-epic joins return before priority derivation.\n\n### Delivery and Queue\n\n- **Request admission.**\n  Each request admits its named lane and unlaned units; absence admits unlaned units. Every survey path carries that request input, with holds and blockers visible.\n- **Unit isolation.**\n  Unrelated malformed rows remain findings without excluding a healthy selected unit.\n- **Queue reports.**\n  Snapshot-only eligible units report lane labels; Lane values preserve Status and assignee decisions. Advance retains those reports.\n\n### Planning and Guidelines\n\n- **Confirmed assignments.**\n  Plan confirms the initiative decision and row map; joined tasks share one lane assignment.\n- **Current ownership rules.**\n  Artifact guidance covers subject state, invariants and shared operations; document tests follow current title rules.\n\n### Caller Contracts\n\n- **One rule home.**\n  Callers bind inputs and route results through linked contracts; report, validation, reservation and recording details live in their owning artifacts. The skill-wide DRY sweep covers all modes, protocols and artifacts.\n\n## References\n\n- **R1.** [Architecture Overview](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-05-1627-caller-contract-dry/architecture-overview.md) — current structure, measured calls and reading order.\n- **R2.** [Agent Review](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-05-1627-caller-contract-dry/agent-review.json) — exact head and target, fixed findings and validation.\n- **R3.** [Criterion Audit](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-05-1627-caller-contract-dry/criterion-audit.md) — all current criteria and historical evidence disposition.\n- **R4.** [Guideline and SOLID Review](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-05-1627-caller-contract-dry/review.md) — complete integration review and validation.\n- **R5.** [Disclosure Observations](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-05-1627-caller-contract-dry/disclosure.md) — fresh-context results, observed failures and scope limits.\n- **R6.** [#1626](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1626) — merged task delivery evidence.\n- **R7.** [#1628](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1628) — merged task delivery evidence.\n- **R8.** [#1629](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1629) — merged task delivery evidence.\n- **R9.** [#1632](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1632) — merged task delivery evidence.\n- **R10.** [#1633](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1633) — merged task delivery evidence.\n- **R11.** [#1634](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1634) — merged task delivery evidence.\n- **R12.** [#1635](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1635) — merged task delivery evidence.\n- **R13.** [#1637](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1637) — merged task delivery evidence.\n- **R14.** [#1638](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1638) — merged task delivery evidence.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T15:48:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T05:50:51Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"m2ux:i17/e03/workspace","ref":"i17/e03/workspace","repo":{"id":1137318642,"node_id":"R_kgDOQ8oa8g","name":"workflow-server","full_name":"m2ux/workflow-server","owner":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for AI agent workflow orchestration. Create high-fidelity, structured workflows that agents discover, navigate, and execute to fulfill user goals.","homepage":"","language":"TypeScript","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":1,"forks":1,"stargazers_count":2,"watchers_count":2,"watchers":2,"open